## Summary

**mrr-incremental-fetch-3sl.6** is implemented and closed. Unlike the previous tickets in this chain, this one had no prior work sitting in the tree — it required building the whole feature:

- **Ungated the board**: removed `isRefreshing` from `baseStack()`/`handleKey()` guards and deleted the full-board spinner overlay from `View`. Every keybinding now works during a refresh.
- **Boot from cache**: `tui.New()` now loads the snapshot via a new `snapStore domain.SnapshotStore` parameter — a warm cache renders the board immediately (any age), a cold cache still shows `stateLoading`.
- **Header age indicator**: spinner + `"14m ago"` collapsing to `"just now"`, backed by a new `headerWidget.SetSnapshotAge`/`ageLabel()`.
- **Closed a real gap**: neither fetch call site was ever passing `Previous` into `mrsvc.FetchOptions`, so the two-phase adapter built in earlier tickets was dead code from the TUI's side — now wired through `Init` and manual refresh, which is what actually makes refreshes fast enough for this feature to matter.
- **Snapshot save-on-swap**: `saveSnapshot()` persists on every successful fetch.

`just check` passes, new unit tests cover the ungating and boot logic, and the mandatory agent-tui gate confirmed all three required scenarios live against the real GitLab-backed binary: cold boot, warm boot with visible spinner+age during an in-flight fetch, arrow-key navigation working mid-fetch, and the label flipping after the swap.

Next up in the epic: `.7` (dirty-set guard) and `.8` (auto-refresh timer), both now unblocked.
